# Copy to secret_internal_api.env in this same folder and fill in a real
# value - generate one with:
#   python -c "import secrets; print(secrets.token_urlsafe(32))"
#
# The same value as mcp_server's, ai_agent's and ember_api's
# secret_internal_api.env - this authenticates service-to-service calls:
# chat_app's MCP sessions to mcp_server and ai_agent (both require it on
# /mcp once they have one), POST /upload, and mcp_server's calls back into
# chat_app (see src/internal_routes.py). There's no human session on those
# requests, so this token is the entire authorization - treat it like a
# password.
INTERNAL_API_TOKEN=
